course: dictionary
lesson: 5923
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. The word marrow can be a part of your body, a vegetable, or a way of saying "completely".
explain: «Red blood cells are made in the bone marrow, the soft middle of big bones.» The clues are bone and soft middle, so marrow means the soft stuff inside bones. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Supper: wild sheep roasted on hot stones, wild duck stuffed with wild rice, marrow-bones of wild oxen.» Marrow-bones are bones with marrow inside, so this is not about a vegetable. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Marrow is a noun, and it has more than one meaning.
fact: Bone marrow is the soft tissue inside bones, and it makes new blood cells.
fact: In the UK, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland, a marrow is a large, long, green vegetable, like a giant courgette.
fact: «Chilled to the marrow» means cold all the way through, completely and deeply.
fact: Some people can donate bone marrow to help save lives.
exercise: In «Red blood cells are made in the bone marrow», what is the marrow? | A type of hot stone | A very cold feeling | *The soft tissue inside bones | A large green vegetable
exercise: Marrows grow big in summer, and people show them at village fairs. What is a marrow in this sentence? | A small, sharp tool | Completely and deeply | *A large, long, green vegetable | The soft tissue inside bones
exercise: What does «chilled to the marrow» mean? | Hungry for a big meal | *Cold all the way through | Covered in green leaves | Slightly cool
test: In «Bone marrow inside many bones makes blood cells», what do the words inside bones tell you? | Marrow is a vegetable that grows in gardens | Marrow is a kind of fruit | Marrow means completely and deeply | *Marrow is the soft stuff inside bones, where blood cells are made
test: Priya says marrow always means a vegetable. Who is right? | *Priya is not right: marrow has more than one meaning, so the clues decide | Nobody, because marrow is not a real word | Priya, because marrow is always a vegetable | Priya is right, but only in the summer
exam: In «bone marrow», the word marrow means | *Soft tissue inside bones | A vegetable | Completely and deeply | A cold feeling
